  "title": "Why Shift Testing Left Part 2: QA Does More After Devs Run Tests",
  "summary": "Shifting left in software testing empowers developers to run tests, speeding up feedback and reducing bugs. QA's role evolves to focus on strategy, automation, and high-level oversight, becoming even more crucial. This approach, akin to past tech shifts like sysadmins moving to cloud systems, embeds QA in development teams, enhancing testing and software quality, while boosting development speed and confidence.",
